# Calendar Safety

Hard rule: no calendar write without `approval_event_id`, `run_id`, and `task_id`.

Additional required fields:

- `plan_version`
- `approved_payload_hash`
- calendar target identifier

The Scheduler can only create draft schedules. Calendar Write Manager is the only writer.

Every write must support:

- dry-run;
- duplicate detection by metadata;
- verification read after write;
- rollback by stored `calendar_event_mapping`.

See `docs/axioms/06-calendar-safety.md`.
